course: dictionary
lesson: 10799
title: Vapour: the invisible gas and the visible mist
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Vapour is a gas that forms when a liquid heats up or slowly evaporates, and water vapour is the most common example. «Evaporation happens at the surface of a liquid at any temperature, when the fastest particles escape as vapour.» The fastest particles break free from the liquid and float away into the air as vapour.
explain: Water vapour is usually invisible, like the air you breathe. «Breathed-out air is warm and full of water vapour, which turns into tiny droplets of mist on cold glass.» The mist you see on a cold window is not the invisible vapour itself: it is tiny drops that formed when the vapour cooled and turned back into liquid.
explain: The same water can be a solid, a liquid or a gas. «For example, the same water can be a hard ice cube, a liquid in a glass, or invisible water vapour in the air.» Water is one substance that changes its form when it gets hotter or colder.
fact: Vapour is a gas made when a liquid is heated or evaporates.
fact: Vapour is often used for tiny drops in the air that you can see, like mist or steam.
fact: Water vapour itself is invisible; the white steam from a kettle is tiny drops that have already cooled and formed.
fact: «Air conditioners drip water outside because cooling the air turns some of its water vapour into droplets.»
fact: Hot vapour, or steam, can burn you, and vapours from glue, paint or cleaning products can be harmful, so use them in fresh air.
exercise: «Breathed-out air is warm and full of water vapour, which turns into tiny droplets of mist on cold glass.» What does this tell you about vapour? | *It can turn back into tiny drops when it cools | It only forms in summer | It is always made of ice | Cold glass turns vapour into solid ice
exercise: «For example, the same water can be a hard ice cube, a liquid in a glass, or invisible water vapour in the air.» Which form of water is invisible? | ice cube | liquid in a glass | *water vapour in the air
exercise: Ella sees white steam rising from a kettle. What is the white steam made of? | *Tiny drops of liquid that you can see | Solid ice crystals falling | Invisible water vapour only | Air with no water in it
test: «Evaporation happens at the surface of a liquid at any temperature, when the fastest particles escape as vapour.» According to this sentence, which particles escape as vapour? | *the fastest particles | the particles in the ice | the slowest particles | the particles in the air
test: «Air conditioners drip water outside because cooling the air turns some of its water vapour into droplets.» Why does the water drip? | Hot air freezes into ice | *Cooling turns some water vapour into droplets | Water falls from the sky into the unit | Air conditioners make water from metal
exam: Which statement is correct? | Vapour only forms in deserts | *Water vapour is an invisible gas, while mist is tiny drops you can see | Vapour and mist are both solid ice | Mist is a gas that you can never see
